     1	# Feature Assembly Plan — F0021: Native React semantic shell + OIDC/session contract and safe re-auth behavior
     2	
     3	**Created:** 2026-11-27
     4	**Author:** Claude / Architect
     5	**Status:** Phase B approved 2026-11-27 by operator token `approve-phase-b` (confirms R1 and R2)
     6	**Plan Run:** 2026-11-27-6cda122a (A+B, new)
     7	**Requirements:** Phase A approved on 2026-11-27 (operator reply recorded as `approve-phase-a`); nine stories, 55 ACs; G1 decisions D1–D4; PM assumptions A1–A8.
     8	**Governing design:** [ADR-0082](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md) (Proposed), refining [ADR-0051](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0051-browser-session-and-revocation-contract.md) (Proposed; decision recorded 2026-11-08). Uses [ADR-0049](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0049-shared-identity-and-verified-principal-boundary.md) for verification and principal resolution, and [ADR-0072](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0072-observatory-is-a-read-only-projection.md) for the route seam.
     9	
    10	## Overview
    11	
    12	Add a backend-for-frontend (BFF) to the engine API process. It handles sign-in, the session cookie, CSRF and origin checks, coalesced renewal, logout with upstream revocation, a session endpoint, and a rejected-credential throttle.
    13	
    14	The work has five parts:
    15	
    16	- **Persistence:** migration 0018 adds four tables and two display-name columns.
    17	- **Identity provider:** the authentik `brain` client becomes confidential.
    18	- **Shell:** `experience/` becomes a React Router shell. It has a route, flag and lazy-loading registry; in-memory session state; one API client; hygiene triggers; and a popup re-authentication flow with explicit re-confirmation.
    19	- **Review Panel:** moves behind the cookie session.
    20	- **Real-browser suite:** proves master blueprint section 121.2 items 8 and 9.
    21	
    22	The existing bearer path, route handlers, authorization and the non-disclosing 404 are unchanged.
    23	
