   110	## Step 1 — Persistence and Settings
   111	
   112	- Migration 0018 follows [migration-design.sql](migration-design.sql). `down_revision` is `0017_f0012_ontology_releases`.
   113	  - The `session_event` append-only trigger reuses `brain_append_only()` from migration 0007.
   114	  - The downgrade refuses when sessions or session events exist.
   115	- `BrowserSessionStore` operations:
   116	  - `start_attempt` and `consume_attempt` (single use);
   117	  - `create_session`: ends the old session as `replaced` or `principal_changed`, in the same transaction;
   118	  - `lookup(cookie_digest)`;
   119	  - `touch`, at most once every 30 s;
   120	  - `renew_locked`: separate transaction, `FOR UPDATE`, `lock_timeout` 15 s;
   121	  - `end` and `record_event`.
   122	- Key ring parsing refuses an empty ring, duplicate key IDs and any key that is not 32 bytes.
   123	
   124	## Step 2 — Identity Provider Client
   125	
   126	- Blueprint changes are as listed above. Feature G0 records the authentik 2026.2 field names for post-logout redirect URIs and refresh-token rotation, and confirms that `default-invalidation-flow` ends the authentik session (R3).
   127	- Dev tooling sends the client secret. The bearer regression suite must pass before Step 3 starts.
   128	
   129	## Step 3 — Sign-in and Callback (S0001)
   130	
   131	**`GET /auth/login`**
   132	
   133	1. Validate `return_to` (ADR-0082 D11), `mode`, `reauth` and `prompt`.
   134	2. Create the attempt with the PKCE verifier, state, nonce and binding.
   135	3. Set `__Host-nebula_login` and redirect to authentik. Discovery failure → 503 `idp_unavailable`.
   136	
   137	**`GET /auth/callback`** — each check fails closed to `/sign-in-failed`, or to the popup failure page.
   138	
   139	1. Throttle check on failure (S0008 AC5).
   140	2. IdP `error` → `idp_error`.
   141	3. State missing, unknown, expired or used → `state_invalid`.
   142	4. Binding cookie digest mismatch → `binding_mismatch`.
   143	5. Code exchange: `client_secret_basic` with the verifier. Failure → `code_exchange_failed`.
   144	6. ID token: signature, issuer, audience, expiry and `nonce` digest. Mismatch → `nonce_mismatch`.
   145	7. Access token through the existing `OidcJwksVerifier`.
   146	8. `PrincipalResolver`: a non-human client or a DISABLED principal is refused with its F0002 reason.
   147	9. Create the session, set the session cookie and clear the login cookie.
   148	10. Redirect to the sanitized route, or render the popup completion page.
   149	
   150	Every failure writes exactly one `authentication_event` and sets no session cookie.
   151	
   152	## Step 4 — Cookie Request Path, CSRF, Throttle (S0002, S0008)
   153	
   154	- Implement the ADR-0082 D5 order in `current_principal`. CSRF and origin checks run in the dependency, before any route handler.
   155	- The throttle (D9) wraps every rejection point: bearer, cookie and callback. The 21st rejection in a window writes one `rate_limited` event; later ones return 429 with `Retry-After` and write nothing.
   156	- Every response to a cookie request carries `Cache-Control: no-store` and `Vary: Cookie`. No CORS middleware is added.
   157	
   158	## Step 5 — Renewal and Lifetime (S0003)
   159	
   160	- Renewal margin is 60 s.
   161	- The lock is a row lock, and the lock owner re-checks the expiry after acquiring it.
   162	- One retry after 500 ms, for network errors and 5xx only. `invalid_grant` ends the session immediately.
   163	- Idle limit 30 min and absolute limit 8 h, enforced at lookup. The absolute limit is never extended.
   164	- `X-Nebula-Activity: background` does not touch the idle deadline.
   165	- Disabled principal or principal mismatch ends the session and returns `401 unauthenticated`.
   166	
   167	## Step 6 — Logout and Session Endpoint (S0005, S0006 server)
   168	
   169	**Logout (ADR-0082 D7)**
   170	
   171	- Takes the same row lock as renewal.
   172	- Revocation uses RFC 7009 with a 5 s timeout and no retry.
   173	- The outcome is recorded in `session_event` `logout`, and the response follows `logout-result-v1`.
   174	- An expired session gives `not_attempted` (`no_live_tokens`).
   175	- A double submit: the second request finds the session ended and returns `not_attempted` (`session_already_ended`), so only one revocation is attempted.
   176	
   177	**Session endpoint and active knowledge base (ADR-0082 D10)**
   178	
   179	- `GET /session` and `PUT /session/active-knowledge-base`.
   180	- `grant_revision` is SHA-256 over the sorted current `(membership_id, grant_revision)` pairs; revoked and expired memberships are excluded.
   181	- Flags are read from `config/experience-flags.yaml`, with an mtime cache.
   182	
   183	## Step 7 — Shell (S0003 AC6, S0004, S0005 AC5/AC6, S0006, S0007)
   184	
   185	**Stack and layout**
   186	
   187	- Stack as ADR-0082 D12.
   188	- Feature-slice folders (SOLUTION-PATTERNS section 5): `src/shell/` for the frame and session, `src/features/review-panel/` for the rehosted panel.
   189	
   190	**Bootstrap**
   191	
   192	1. `GET /api/session`.
   193	2. On 401, `location.assign('/api/auth/login?return_to=' + current route)`.
   194	3. On 200, validate the body with the generated AJV validator and store it in the Zustand session store, in memory.
   195	
   196	**API client**
   197	
   198	- One `apiClient` handles every request. It maps the D5 outcomes and never retries an unsafe method.
   199	- `401 session_expired`:
   200	  - unsafe request → push it to the blocked queue (label, method, route, body; memory only);
   201	  - GET → mark it for one retry;
   202	  - then open `SessionExpiredDialog`.
   203	- `403 csrf_rejected`: refetch the session to refresh the CSRF token, then show an inline error. No retry.
   204	
   205	**Re-authentication (ADR-0082 D8)**
   206	
   207	- Popup with a `ref`. The completion signal is accepted from BroadcastChannel or `postMessage`, only from the shell's own origin and only with the pending `ref`.
   208	- After the signal, `GET /session`:
   209	  - same principal → retry blocked GETs once, then `ReconfirmDialog` with "Submit now" or "Cancel" for each blocked mutation;
   210	  - different principal → discard the work, run hygiene, go to Home.
   211	- A blocked popup, or one closed without completing, offers "Sign in on this page", with the lost-input warning.
   212	
   213	**Hygiene and cross-tab**
   214	
   215	- `hygiene.reset()`:
   216	  - aborts every registered request;
   217	  - calls `queryClient.clear()`;
   218	  - resets resource stores;
   219	  - is awaited before rendering the new state.
   220	- Triggers: sign-out, principal change, active knowledge-base change, `grant_revision` change.
   221	- Cross-tab: BroadcastChannel messages, plus a background session poll every 30 s while the page is visible and on focus.
   222	
   223	**Idle warning**
   224	
   225	- Shown from `idle_expires_at − idle_warning_seconds`, against server time.
   226	- "Stay signed in" sends one user-initiated `GET /api/session` without the background header.
   227	
   228	**Route registry and Review Panel**
   229	
   230	- Registry entries are `{path, flagKey, lazy}`.
   231	  - Flag off or unknown: not-found screen, no module request, not shown in navigation.
   232	  - Module load failure: `RouteLoadError` with a retry.
   233	- The Review Panel route is `/reviews/:reviewItemId`. Engine paths, behavior and receipts are unchanged.
   234	- A `token` query parameter is removed with `history.replaceState` before anything else runs, and its value is never read or sent anywhere.
   235	
   236	**Accessibility, language and budget**
   237	
   238	- WCAG 2.2 AA with semantic theme tokens. All strings come from `en-US.json`.
   239	- Budget script: the entry chunk's initial JavaScript must be at most 180 kB gzip, measured from the Vite manifest.
   240	
   241	## Step 8 — Real-Browser Proof (S0009)
   242	
   243	**Stack and run conditions**
   244	
   245	- `docker-compose.e2e.yml` starts:
   246	  - PostgreSQL and authentik from the dev blueprint;
   247	  - the engine, with `BRAIN_OIDC_BACKCHANNEL_URL` pointing at `idp-recorder`;
   248	  - the built shell under `vite preview` on 4173.
   249	- Runs start from a clean volume. Results record the authentik, Chromium and Playwright versions.
   250	
   251	**Proofs**
   252	
   253	- **Token absence (S0009 AC1):** inspect cookies, every storage API, every URL, and every response body and header.
   254	- **Single refresh (AC2):** the recorder counts refresh grants per refresh-token family while 20 parallel requests run against an expired access token. The test-only `BRAIN_TEST_ACCESS_SKEW` setting is absent outside the e2e composition, and startup refuses it when `BRAIN_PUBLIC_ORIGIN` is not localhost.
   255	- **Revocation failure (AC3):** the recorder injects a 503 or a drop on `/revoke`. A follow-up refresh grant with the revoked token is refused by authentik.
   256	- **Principal isolation (AC4):** alice and bob; a list of malicious return routes.
   257	- **Mutation continuity (AC5):** a Review Panel decision is blocked by an expired session, is not received (the engine decision count is unchanged), and is sent only on "Submit now". A stale or revoked variant is refused without retry.
   258	
   259	## Acceptance Criteria to Implementation / Proof Map
   260	
   261	| Story / AC | Step | Proof |
   262	|---|---|---|
   263	| S0001 AC1 | 3 | Login redirect carries `code_challenge_method=S256`, state and nonce; attempt row holds digests and ciphertext only; no verifier or nonce in any response |
   264	| S0001 AC2 | 3 | Callback success test: cookie attributes asserted (`__Host-`, Secure, HttpOnly, Lax, Path=/, no Domain, 256-bit value); session row with the resolved principal |
   265	| S0001 AC3 | 3, 8 | API tests scan bodies and headers; e2e storage, cookie and URL scan |
   266	| S0001 AC4 | 3 | One fixture for each failure reason; zero sessions; no session cookie; one `authentication_event` each; failure page text has no reason |
   267	| S0001 AC5 | 3, 8 | `return_routes` unit table (absolute, `//`, backslash, encoded, unregistered → `/`); e2e malicious list |
   268	| S0001 AC6 | 3 | Non-human `azp` and DISABLED principal fixtures → failure page, reason recorded |
   269	| S0001 AC7 | 3, 7 | Same principal: old cookie → 401 at once. Different principal: old session `principal_changed` and the shell hygiene test |
   270	| S0002 AC1 | 4 | Cookie request to `/reviews`, `/content` and `/facts` reaches the handler under the session principal; verifier and resolver call order asserted |
   271	| S0002 AC2 | 4 | Matrix: missing or wrong token, foreign Origin, missing Origin and Referer, Referer fallback, `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site` → 403 `csrf_rejected`; handler spy not called; zero writes; event cause recorded |
   272	| S0002 AC3 | 4 | Cross-site GET answered under normal authorization; no `Access-Control-*` headers |
   273	| S0002 AC4 | 4, 5 | Distinct codes: unauthenticated, session_expired (idle, absolute, renewal), denial = existing 404 with the session still valid afterwards (R1), csrf 403 |
   274	| S0002 AC5 | 4, 7 | Cookie plus `Authorization` → 400 `ambiguous_credentials`; shell lint rule and client test confirm no `Authorization` header |
   275	| S0002 AC6 | 4 | Existing bearer suites pass unchanged |
   276	| S0003 AC1 | 5 | Expired access token → one refresh, request served, `Set-Cookie` absent |
   277	| S0003 AC2 | 5, 8 | Two-worker PostgreSQL test with N concurrent requests → one token-endpoint call (stub) and all succeed or all `session_expired`; e2e recorder count = 1 |
   278	| S0003 AC3 | 5, 8 | Rotated refresh token stored atomically; each failure kind ends the session, writes `renewal_failed` and returns 401 |
   279	| S0003 AC4 | 5 | Frozen-clock idle test; background header does not extend the deadline |
   280	| S0003 AC5 | 5 | 8 h absolute limit despite activity and renewals; no renewal attempted after it |
   281	| S0003 AC6 | 7 | Component test: warning at 28 min (server time), countdown, "Stay signed in" sends one request, dismissing changes nothing |
   282	| S0004 AC1 | 7 | Client test: page and input kept; dialog lists blocked mutations as "not submitted"; zero retries |
   283	| S0004 AC2 | 7, 8 | Popup flow; completion signal carries only `ref`; dialog closes with input intact |
   284	| S0004 AC3 | 7, 8 | GET retried once; mutation sent only on "Submit now"; "Cancel" discards it |
   285	| S0004 AC4 | 7, 8 | Re-confirmed request carries the new CSRF token; stale or revoked variant → engine 404 or 409 shown in context, no retry; engine audit row present |
   286	| S0004 AC5 | 7, 8 | Different principal → work and queue discarded, hygiene, Home; e2e principal isolation |
   287	| S0004 AC6 | 7 | Blocked popup → "Sign in on this page" with the warning; storage spy shows no input written |
